Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:03:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui completion obligations: docstrings cover
 Desktop, never-reopened-chat note, settle_started in-memory precheck

Follow-up of PR #2159 (review 5890472426, non-blocking nits), card t_01a1d4c0fc17d36d.

1. ProcessObligationMixin and the ProcessCheckpointMixin._recover_owed_completions_locked stub
   documented gateway completions only; they now cover Desktop (owner: tui) obligations too.
2. Module docstrings (process_registry_obligations.py, tui_gateway/completion_obligation.py) state that a
   tui obligation for a chat never reopened (deleted/archived) is re-armed and wakes that chat on each
   Desktop start until OBLIGATION_MAX_RECOVERIES / OBLIGATION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS drops it (bounded by design).
3. settle_started read the receipt file under the registry lock for every offered pid on every notice-turn
   start, even for jobs that never carried an obligation. The registry now keeps `_tui_owed`, the ids this
   process wrote (receipt writer, `_completion_obligation`) or re-armed (`_recover_owed_completions_locked`)
   a tui obligation for, and `settle_tui_completion` answers any other id from memory. An id leaves the set
   once its receipt no longer owes it, so a failed settle write is still retried.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_tui_completion_obligation.py::
test_notice_turn_start_reads_only_receipts_this_backend_owes spies on receipt_path: RED on the old code
("a pid with no owed tui obligation must not touch its receipt"), GREEN with the fix; it also proves a
re-armed obligation in a fresh backend is still settled. test_tui_completion_obligation.py and
test_process_completion_receipt_nits.py: 29 passed.
